WEBVTT

00:07:57.587 --> 00:08:01.164
but letting them out
really may be the better move.

00:08:01.188 --> 00:08:02.381
Keeping them inside

00:08:02.405 --> 00:08:05.894
can amplify our feelings
of anger or sadness.

00:08:06.759 --> 00:08:09.180
And while we're releasing those tears,

00:08:09.204 --> 00:08:12.065
our hormones inside,
they're on high alert,

00:08:12.089 --> 00:08:13.704
and we know this

00:08:13.728 --> 00:08:16.736
because of Dr. William Frey, a biochemist.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.085
He found that inside
of our emotional tears --

00:08:19.109 --> 00:08:20.934
not our everyday, like, yawning tears,

00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:22.680
but our emotional tears --

00:08:22.704 --> 00:08:25.873
there's high concentrations
of stress hormones

00:08:25.897 --> 00:08:27.262
and leucine enkephalins,

00:08:27.286 --> 00:08:29.960
which, easier on my tongue, is endorphins.